@SmartX.Api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7002

### register an environmental sensor
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01",
  "location": { "zone": "Zone 1", "room": "Sub-Zone B", "nodeId": "N01" },
  "category": "Environmental"
}

### register a power consumption sensor
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02",
  "location": { "zone": "Zone 1", "room": "Facility A", "nodeId": "N02" },
  "category": "PowerConsumption"
}

### registering the same mac again should 409
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:01",
  "location": { "zone": "Zone 1", "room": "Sub-Zone B", "nodeId": "N01" },
  "category": "Environmental"
}

### a malformed mac address should 400
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "not-a-mac",
  "location": { "zone": "Zone 1", "room": "Sub-Zone B", "nodeId": "N03" },
  "category": "Actuator"
}

### list every registered sensor
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors

### look up a sensor that exists
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01

### look up a mac that was never registered, should 404
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors/00:00:00:00:00:00

### a valid deployment tree with one registered sensor leaf, should be valid
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/deployment/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Zone 1",
  "children": [
    {
      "name": "Sub-Zone B",
      "children": [
        { "name": "Moisture Sensor 01", "sensorMacAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### a tree pointing at a sensor that was never registered
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/deployment/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Zone 1",
  "children": [
    { "name": "Ghost Sensor", "sensorMacAddress": "FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF" }
  ]
}

### two siblings sharing a name should be reported
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/deployment/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Zone 1",
  "children": [
    { "name": "Sub-Zone B" },
    { "name": "sub-zone b" }
  ]
}

### a malformed body should 400, not 500
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/deployment/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ this is not valid json

### register an actuator sensor, needed for the telemetry requests below
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:03",
  "location": { "zone": "Zone 1", "room": "Sub-Zone B", "nodeId": "N03" },
  "category": "Actuator"
}

### usage on a sensor that has not reported yet, should be 200 with zeroed counters
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/usage

### post a valid moisture reading
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01",
  "value": 42.5
}

### post a valid power reading
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02",
  "value": 400
}

### post a valid valve state
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:03",
  "state": true
}

### posting to an unregistered mac should 400
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "00:00:00:00:00:00",
  "value": 50
}

### a moisture reading out of range should 400
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01",
  "value": 150
}

### a negative wattage should 400
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02",
  "value": -10
}

### a mixed batch, 2 valid and 2 rejected, should 200 with accepted 2 and rejected 2
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01", "value": 41.0 },
  { "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02", "value": 420 },
  { "macAddress": "00:00:00:00:00:00", "value": 50 },
  { "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01", "value": 999 }
]

### the moisture sensor's recent readings, in the flat dashboard shape
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01

### the moisture sensor's usage, should now show one live reading
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/usage

### recent readings for an unregistered mac should 404
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/00:00:00:00:00:00

### every sensor with its latest reading in one call, confirms overview isnt swallowed by the {macAddress} route
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/overview

### health for the moisture sensor after a couple of ordinary readings, should be normal
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/health

### health for a sensor that has never reported, every window should be silent
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:04",
  "location": { "zone": "Zone 1", "room": "Sub-Zone B", "nodeId": "N04" },
  "category": "PowerConsumption"
}

### the never-reported sensor's health, should show status silent and no seconds since last reading
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:04/health

### post a small reading, then a jump past the 50w threshold, to script a spike
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:04",
  "value": 100
}

###
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:04",
  "value": 200
}

### that sensor's health should now show a spike window and overall status spike
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:04/health

### health for an unregistered mac should 404
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/00:00:00:00:00:00/health

### the overview now embeds each sensor's whole health, including the scripted spike above
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry/overview

### list attachments for a sensor, empty until something is uploaded (curl -F is used for the actual upload)
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/attachments

### listing attachments for an unregistered mac should 404
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors/00:00:00:00:00:00/attachments

### downloading an attachment that does not exist should 404
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/attachments/00000000000000000000000000000000

### deleting an attachment that does not exist should 404
DELETE {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/sensors/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/attachments/00000000000000000000000000000000

### the command stream snapshot, queue depth plus every device the processor has seen
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/stream/snapshot

### the same devices narrowed by a piece of a mac address
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/stream/devices?search=EE:03

### post a reading with the radio fields so the stream has rssi, hops and protocol to show
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:03",
  "state": false,
  "rssi": -71,
  "hopCount": 2,
  "dutyCycle": 1.5,
  "packetLoss": 0.8,
  "protocol": "Zigbee"
}

### open the valve by hand
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:03", "open": true }

### a command to a moisture sensor should 400
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01", "open": true }

### a command to an unregistered mac should 404
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "00:00:00:00:00:00", "open": true }

### what a valve would be told next, 200 once and then 204, an unregistered mac gives 404
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/commands/pending/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:03

### the overrides that can be undone, newest first
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/commands/history

### undo the newest override, a second undo with nothing left should 409
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/commands/undo

### what a device reported, oldest first, add from and to as ISO times to narrow it
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/stream/devices/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/history

### a device the stream has not heard from should 404
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/stream/devices/00:00:00:00:00:00/history

### a start after the end should 400
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/stream/devices/AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01/history?from=2030-01-02T00:00:00Z&to=2030-01-01T00:00:00Z

### a valve reporting its own fault, raises a critical alert named after the code
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{ "macAddress": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02", "state": false, "fault": "StuckValve" }

### close every open valve as one override, one undo puts them all back
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/commands/close-all

### only the pumps and valves the stream has heard from
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/stream/devices?category=Actuator

### only devices with an active fault or gone quiet, narrowed again by mac text
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/stream/devices?alertsOnly=true&category=Actuator&search=02


### what needs attention and what has usually followed the last thing that happened
GET {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/insights

### tell the engine about a search, after this it should suggest opening valve-b1
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/insights/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:05" }

### blank search text should 400
POST {{SmartX.Api_HostAddress}}/api/insights/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "  " }
